[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1511","stub":{"id":"1511","section":"2) Bedrock Campground to Fall Creek Reservoir","altname":"","river":"Fall Creek","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-ORE"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"238","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:10:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The put in is at the bridge just downstream of Bedrock day use site. There are multiple options to put in, but most opt for the 8-10ft seal launch off the rocks just across the bridge, on river right, and just downstream of the bridge. The next mile or so is more or less gorged in bedrock until the river leaves the old burn area and enters the forest.","id":"111795","location":{"latitude":"43.971901","longitude":"-122.544998"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":"Fh8BklijE4wpCj5YaYrxh","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Roughly 8 miles upstream of the Put-in at Bedrock Campground, there is a roadside drop about 8-10 feet in height. It requires the run below to be on the high end to be in, but offers a clean lip, a sloping bedrock landing and a moving pool run-out. It is very lapable and has a fire ring. Look for it on the left hand side of the road about 8 miles up from Bedrock. As of 11/5/2022 access is restricted due to the Gale fire cleanup from 2021. The road is closed about 5 miles up from bedrock and there is a lot of activity from forest workers. It is unclear if the falls and surrounding forest was impacted by the fire, but it's likely. Photo is from 2019 at a runnable flow.","id":"88umfrccR2QVHcLKxXl06","location":{"latitude":"43.984547","longitude":"-122.446102"},"name":"8mile - Bonus Drop","distance":"0","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"t6fg9SxspQgdjqwIRTlha"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Not far below the put in the river constricts and presents paddlers with a small but powerful ledge hole at high flows. Stickier on the right. Below this drop there is a long recovery pool, but it is fairly gorged in so collecting gear from a swimmer might be challenging.","id":"r9Nvxy5htn0wu5utudlyH","location":{"latitude":"43.973392","longitude":"-122.549104"},"name":"Ledge Hole","distance":"0.25","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"upNq8AlfvlBMNQ8nd9SvR"},{"type":"portage","description":"Logjam visible from the road 11/5/2022. Scout ahead of time and make a plan. A small class II rapid leads right into the jam. Easy walk on the right. Location in the map is approximate.","id":"aDyexu0CyDGdi4p8ASncb","location":{"latitude":"43.972553","longitude":"-122.573376"},"name":"Log Jam / Portage","distance":"1.6","photoID":"157e2pkdfOEIWA6Cqj5GL","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Fish Ramp is the Crux of the run and is class IV at medium levels and up. It is a rather unique rapid and appropraitely named, as a concrete boat ramp enters from the left immediately at the bottom of the rapid. I am told it is, or was, used in fish collection and relocation efforts around the Fall Creek reservoir. It's mostly a long low angle rock slide with a hole in the middle, and an intimidating looking pilow on the right that becomes an explosed rock with water splashing up on it at lower flows. The line is mostly down the middle, avoiding the rocks on the left and right at the bottom. At the time of this writing, there is some wood on the right behind the big boulder at the bottom as well. A long recovery pool follows this rapid. This is also a convenient takeout location. Below this rapid the run is mostly class II with ample flat water until you get to the takeout rapids at the reservoir.","id":"7A5P2Vvz5oLXep3Orpc1f","location":{"latitude":"43.96704","longitude":"-122.629822"},"name":"Fish Ramp Rapid ","distance":"5.34","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"SZL0KKc1TMJJGtZA3ztHm"},{"type":"takeout","description":"There are two takeouts most paddlers use. This one is the furthest downstream and is where the river meets the reservoir. There are two rapids here that are optional. One is leading into and directly under the bridge, and the other is a bit downstream. You can scout both on the way up.","id":"117067","location":{"latitude":"43.972301","longitude":"-122.660004"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8","photoID":"PBvcGupFyEd0RVVMMPU3H","difficulty":"III","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"vueWTitzhoZrfFieHRROY","title":"Portage in the first half of the run","post_date":"2022-11-06 06:32:58+00","detail":"There is a river-wide logjam in the first half of the run shortly after crossing under the main road ( so that the road is back on river right) after leaving the burn area. Easy scout from the road on your shuttle, and easy walk on river right.","user":{"name":"Clinton Begley"}}],"photos":[{"id":"157e2pkdfOEIWA6Cqj5GL","ext":"jpg","post_id":"eTCju2gug7RJHDVyx3hTo","description":"Portage ","caption":"Portage Mid-way into the run. Visible roadside. ","poi_name":null,"subject":"Portage ","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-11-05T06:22:19.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:22:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/157e2pkdfOEIWA6Cqj5GL","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/157e2pkdfOEIWA6Cqj5GL"}},{"id":"PBvcGupFyEd0RVVMMPU3H","ext":"jpg","post_id":"eTCju2gug7RJHDVyx3hTo","description":"","caption":"Takeout Rapid at Reservoir ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":"117067","photo_date":"2022-11-05T06:22:19.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:22:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/PBvcGupFyEd0RVVMMPU3H","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/PBvcGupFyEd0RVVMMPU3H"}},{"id":"SZL0KKc1TMJJGtZA3ztHm","ext":"jpg","post_id":"eTCju2gug7RJHDVyx3hTo","description":"Stay center and avoid the big rock, and hole, and wood, on the right. ","caption":"The Crux of Fish Ramp ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":"7A5P2Vvz5oLXep3Orpc1f","photo_date":"2022-11-05T06:22:19.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:22:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/SZL0KKc1TMJJGtZA3ztHm","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/SZL0KKc1TMJJGtZA3ztHm"}},{"id":"Fh8BklijE4wpCj5YaYrxh","ext":"jpg","post_id":"eTCju2gug7RJHDVyx3hTo","description":"","caption":"View from the put-in bridge at Bedrock Campground ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":"111795","photo_date":"2022-11-05T06:22:19.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:22:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/Fh8BklijE4wpCj5YaYrxh","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/Fh8BklijE4wpCj5YaYrxh"}},{"id":"MzGqNZa4QOSirt2Y6iHXa","ext":"jpg","post_id":"eTCju2gug7RJHDVyx3hTo","description":"","caption":"View from the Ramp at Fish Ramp Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":"7A5P2Vvz5oLXep3Orpc1f","photo_date":"2022-11-05T06:22:19.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:22:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/MzGqNZa4QOSirt2Y6iHXa","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/MzGqNZa4QOSirt2Y6iHXa"}},{"id":"t6fg9SxspQgdjqwIRTlha","ext":"jpg","post_id":"NvE7ctZr7eG69KeabKDY6","description":"8 miles upstream of Bedrock Campground","caption":"Fall Creek Bonus Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":"88umfrccR2QVHcLKxXl06","photo_date":"2019-01-24T06:31:00.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:31:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/t6fg9SxspQgdjqwIRTlha","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/t6fg9SxspQgdjqwIRTlha"}},{"id":"upNq8AlfvlBMNQ8nd9SvR","ext":"jpg","post_id":"eTCju2gug7RJHDVyx3hTo","description":"A nice ledge hole is barely visible upstream. This can be rather stout and is best run on the left at high flows, or boof the seam anywhere in the center to right. ","caption":"About 1/4 into the run through the old burn before you get to the forest ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Clinton Begley","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-11-05T06:22:19.000Z","updated_at":"2022-11-06T06:22:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/upNq8AlfvlBMNQ8nd9SvR","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/upNq8AlfvlBMNQ8nd9SvR"}}],"detail":{"id":"1511","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This is above the Fall Creek Reservoir.\n\nEach fall the USACE draws down the reservoir to aid out-migrating Pacific Lamprey amocetes November to December. The I-II stretch below the reservoir gets a bump, but it has no impact on the inflow upstream of the reservoir which this listing describes.\n\nTo determine the water in this run, you must look at the INFLOW to the Fall Creek Reservoir, available on the USACE website here: [http://www.nwd-wc.usace.army.mil/dd/common/projects/www/fal.html](http://www.nwd-wc.usace.army.mil/dd/common/projects/www/fal.html)\n\nWhen it's raining, there is a correlation between the outflow below the reservoir and the inflow above it, so the linked gauge here can be useful. But it's not a 1:1 and the inflow to the lake should be checked to be sure before making the drive.\n\n -Clinton 10/26/2018","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"7.3","correlations":[{"reachID":"1511","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"800","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"nam